From: Ruizhi Zhong <ruizhi.zhong88@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 03 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] honour STRATA_PACKAGE_MANAGED=1 in install and update

Strata acquires things in two ways: `strata install` hands over to the installer
of a full source folder (pip, the engine, the models), and `strata update` /
`strata components update|rollback|install-file|use|remove` download or move
engines inside the component folder. Under Portage both are wrong: this ebuild
merges the engine as a component package, so a self-update would write files the
package database does not know about and leave the installed component
mismatched with what Portage recorded.

The launcher installed by the ebuild exports STRATA_PACKAGE_MANAGED=1. When it
is set, the commands that write are refused with exit code 5 and name Portage
instead, while `rollback`, `install-file`, `use` and `remove` still work when
they are pointed at a folder the calling user owns (--components-dir /
STRATA_COMPONENTS_DIR), which keeps per-user engine experiments possible without
touching /usr. Read-only operations are left alone: `update --check` still reads
the feed and reports the version emerge would install, `components engines`
still lists what is installed.

This is a guard on the normal entry point, not a sandbox: the variable is set by
the launcher, so running strata.py from another wrapper does not inherit it. A
user who wants the upstream behaviour back can export
STRATA_PACKAGE_MANAGED=0.

Upstream status: not submitted; Gentoo packaging only.
---
--- a/strata_cli/cli.py
+++ b/strata_cli/cli.py
@@ -2074,6 +2074,10 @@
     """The one place the terminal acquires anything: it hands over to the installer (setup.py) of a full Strata
     folder, which is where pip, the engine and the models are fetched. A folder without it (the terminal archive)
     says so and names what to do instead."""
+    if os.environ.get("STRATA_PACKAGE_MANAGED") == "1":
+        return _error("this Strata is installed and managed by Portage (sci-ml/strata): the engine is updated "
+                      "with emerge, not `strata install`. Set STRATA_PACKAGE_MANAGED=0 to run this folder's "
+                      "installer anyway.", 5)
     installer = Path(os.environ.get("STRATA_INSTALL_DIR") or ROOT) / "setup.py"
     if not installer.is_file():
         return _error("this folder has no installer (setup.py). Engines, models and updates are installed from a "
--- a/strata_cli/update_cmd.py
+++ b/strata_cli/update_cmd.py
@@ -270,6 +270,14 @@
     return chosen if found else own
 
 
+def _component_dir_user_owned(path: Path) -> bool:
+    """A component folder the current user may write to: it exists and is writable, or its parent is (so it can be created)."""
+    if path.exists():
+        return path.is_dir() and os.access(path, os.W_OK)
+    parent = path.parent
+    return parent.exists() and os.access(parent, os.W_OK)
+
+
 def run(a) -> int:
     from strata_control import acquisition, engine_component as ec, feed as feedmod, signing, updater
     machine = a.output in ("json", "jsonl")
@@ -281,6 +289,20 @@
             print(f"strata: {message}", file=sys.stderr)
         return code
 
+    if os.environ.get("STRATA_PACKAGE_MANAGED") == "1":
+        sub = getattr(a, "components_command", None)
+        # `--check` only reads the feed: it names the version emerge would install and changes nothing
+        if (a.command == "update" or sub == "update") and not getattr(a, "check", False):
+            return fail("this Strata is installed and managed by Portage (sci-ml/strata); update the engine "
+                        "with emerge, not `strata update`. Set STRATA_PACKAGE_MANAGED=0 to use the self-update "
+                        "feed anyway.", 5)
+        if sub in ("rollback", "install-file", "use", "remove"):
+            target = Path(a.components_dir) if a.components_dir else None
+            if target is None or not _component_dir_user_owned(target):
+                return fail("this Strata is installed and managed by Portage (sci-ml/strata); the system "
+                            "component folder is read-only. To switch to, delete, roll back to or install an "
+                            "engine file, pass --components-dir pointing at a folder you own (and set "
+                            "STRATA_COMPONENTS_DIR to it), or set STRATA_PACKAGE_MANAGED=0.", 5)
     root = Path(a.components_dir) if a.components_dir else default_components_dir(ec)
     try:
         hardware = updater.detect_hardware()
